"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-01T07:58:01Z","updated_at":"2025-04-01T07:59:35Z","body":"> This should be project setting, otherwise it's making camera textures completely unusable in the editor, since it's spamming errors non stop.\r\n\r\nI predicted this may happen 😅\r\nI considered making it a project setting, but I think it would be better if the editor itself activated and deactivated camera feed monitoring on demand. That would make it seamless for the user.\r\nI could have a look myself in the coming days, but I'm not sure where best to insert the handlers so I'd also be happy for some help :)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2768510485/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2768521260","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104232#issuecomment-2768521260","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104232","id":2768521260,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lBEgs","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-01T08:02:24Z","updated_at":"2025-04-01T08:02:24Z","body":"Yes, it might be better to activate it automatically, when feed is requested. Not sure if there's much purpose in deactivating it, it makes sense to have it inactive by default to decrease start time, but deactivating probably won't do much.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2768521260/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2768550752","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104232#issuecomment-2768550752","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104232","id":2768550752,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lBLtg","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-01T08:14:13Z","updated_at":"2025-04-01T08:14:13Z","body":"We use project setting to enable text-to-speech, for the same startup time reason, but I guess it might be better to init it on demand as well, instead of printing errors.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2768550752/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2778298165","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104232#issuecomment-2778298165","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104232","id":2778298165,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lmXc1","user":{"login":"j20001970","id":71766835,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNzY2ODM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71766835?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970","html_url":"https://github.com/j20001970","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-04T10:48:42Z","updated_at":"2025-04-04T10:48:42Z","body":"> It may be appropriate to move the `CameraServer` to a GDExtension because it is very self-contained, and it is questionable that code to monitor cameras even ships with all Godot games in the first place.\r\n\r\nAgree that it would be unnecessary to actively monitor available cameras when most of games do not use them at all, but I think it's worth keeping the abstraction part of `CameraServer` and `CameraFeed` for the consistent interface across different platforms, and letting GDExtension/GDNative plugins implement functionalities that are platform-specific, similar to how Godot ARCore plugin implements `XRInterface` for `XRServer`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2778298165/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]